USC: don't flatten conditional arms containing memory loads

CanPredicate refused to predicate the hardware load instructions but not
ILOADMEMCONST, which every OpenCL MEMLD becomes before finalisation.  So an
arm holding a load could be flattened, and with the MOVC form both arms run
unconditionally: "p == 0 ? 1 : p[0]" loaded from a null pointer and faulted
the GPU.  Treat ILOADMEMCONST like the other loads.

diff --git a/tools/intern/usc2/iselect.c b/tools/intern/usc2/iselect.c
index 034dcfe..0457046 100644
--- a/tools/intern/usc2/iselect.c
+++ b/tools/intern/usc2/iselect.c
@@ -13365,7 +13365,13 @@ static IMG_BOOL CanPredicate(PINTERMEDIATE_STATE psState,
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (eOpcode == ILDAB ||
+	/*
+		ILOADMEMCONST is an OpenCL global memory load: flattening its arm into
+		a MOVC would run it unconditionally, and a guarded load (a null or
+		out-of-range pointer) then faults the GPU.
+	*/
+	if (eOpcode == ILOADMEMCONST ||
+	eOpcode == ILDAB ||
 	eOpcode == ILDAW ||
 	eOpcode == ILDAD ||
 	eOpcode == ILDLD ||
